# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# modular-sUAS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Parametric sweep output. Regenerable by re-running fuselage_variants.py, and
# large: variant_output alone is ~2.4 GB across 576 parts. The pattern covers the
# _original and _baseline copies kept as references.
#
# Each of those directories also holds its own .gitignore containing `*`, which
# matches the .gitignore itself -- so those files were never committed and the
# protection existed only in one working tree. Ignoring from here instead makes it
# part of the repository, and those nested files can be deleted.
variant_output*/

# Scratch output from test_fuse.ipynb -- one-off renders, ~106 MB.
test_fuse_output/

# In-flight renders. solid_render writes to <name>.partial.stl and moves it into
# place only after OpenSCAD exits zero, so a leftover means an interrupted run
# rather than a finished part. The name must end in .stl because OpenSCAD selects
# its export format from the extension.
*.partial.stl
*.partial.scad

# Snapshots from scad_snapshot.py: build artifacts, ~0.5 MB each, regenerate rather
# than commit.
scad_snapshot*.json

# Blender writes a .blend1 backup beside every save.
*.blend1

# Explorer thumbnail caches. Previously only ignored via a machine-local global
# gitignore, so they reappeared for anyone else.
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
src/Fuselage/variant_output/

# Everything the freecad/ scripts write. They used to save beside themselves, which put
# .FCStd documents, .step exports, check meshes and a 14 MB preview/ tree in among the
# geometry modules -- and got corner_tree.FCStd plus its rotating .FCStd1 backup committed,
# 440 KB of binary rewritten on every check run. corner_common.out_path() and
# render_variant.py's DEFAULT_OUT both point here now.
src/Fuselage/freecad/out/

# FreeCAD documents and their rotating backups, wherever they land. The same case as
# *.blend1 above: .FCStd1 is the previous save, renamed on every write. The sweep's real
# .FCStd deliverable (UC-2, IP-FC-14) goes to variant_output/, already ignored.
*.FCStd
*.FCStd[0-9]
